        "title": "fix(status): hide healthy plugin summary",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where compact `/status` output included a `Plugins: OK` row that conveyed no actionable information and could be mistaken for a plugin name.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nHealthy compact plugin status now renders no row. Plugin errors, quarantines, dependency issues, and health-collection failures remain visible; `/status plugins` retains its detailed healthy summary and inventory.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCompact `/status` output is less noisy and less ambiguous without hiding plugin problems.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `corepack pnpm test src/status/status-plugin-health.test.ts` — 18 tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_CHECK_CHANGED_REMOTE_CHILD=1 OPENCLAW_CHANGED_LANES_RAW_SYNC=1 corepack pnpm check:changed` — passed.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox: `tbx_01kwr0kfb4spa0nnmsmezbffsm`; Actions run 28726579046.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n",
